<title>UK: Dobbies Garden Centres sets debut premium.</title>
<headline>Dobbies Garden Centres sets debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dobbies Garden Centres plc set a premium on their first day of trade on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Monday.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 265p by 1510 GMT, ahead of the 200p placing price, although no trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The placing, sponsored by Bell Lawrie White, raised 2.5 million stg and valued the company, which operates garden centres in central Scotland and the north east of England, at 9.4 million.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
